hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"980","We told us Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, Ibn Wahb told us that Malik told him, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, Muhammad bin Idris told us. Al-Shafi’i, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Rabi’, said: Al-Shafi’i said, Malik told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he was asked about the prayer Fear, he said: “The imam and a group of people will stand up and lead them in prayer one rak’ah, and a group will be between him and the enemy and they will not pray, so when those with him pray One rak'ah, they delayed in place of those who had not prayed, and they did not greet, and those who had not prayed came forward and prayed one rak'ah with him, then the imam departed, and he had prayed two rak'ahs, then each one of the two groups stands and prays one rak'ah for themselves. If the fear is greater than that, they pray as men standing Their feet and knees, facing the Qiblah or not facing it.” Nafi’ said: I do not see Ibn Umar mentioning it except on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"981","Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Ishaq bin Isa al-Tabbaa’ narrated to us, Malik informed us of this chain of narration alike, and he said: Nafi’ said: Ibn Umar narrated that. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace"
